/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  thermoPhysPropDict (v2) -- T8: the aqueous activity SURFACE for a sour-water
  brine.  Ionic AND molecular activities come from the truncated Pitzer
  expansion of Edwards, Maurer, Newman & Prausnitz (1978) on the molality
  basis.

  This is a model-CONTRAST case, like pitzer_calcite_brine: the operations
  carry an explicit per-op `activityModel` so the two models can be read
  against each other on ONE feed.  The contrast here is not a matter of
  accuracy -- it is a matter of what each model CAN SAY.  Davies is a
  charge-only correlation: for a neutral solute it returns exactly 1, always,
  and therefore cannot express salting-out at all.  Edwards' truncation keeps
  molecule-molecule and molecule-ion terms, so dissolved NH3 and CO2 get a
  gamma that moves with the brine around them.

  The analysis lives in the OPERATIONS; the species and reactions live in the
  curated chemistry tree; the interaction parameters live under
  parameters/EdwardsPitzer/ with the paper's own caveat on every record
  ("preliminary results subject to change as more and better data become
  available").
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

recordType    thermophysicalPropertySystem;
schemaVersion 2;

components ( water );

aqueousProperties
{
    activityCoefficients
    {
        model          EdwardsPitzer;
        referenceBasis aqueousMolality;
    }
}
